<!--
  The APP's own words.

  Everything here belongs to the PERSON using the app, not to any one book,
  so it follows the device language the way every reader app does: a Russian
  novel on an English Kindle does not turn the menus Russian. Strings that are
  typeset INTO a book - the block labels, the words the EPUB carries - live in
  BOOK_CHROME_STRINGS instead and are translated per course.

  Plain resources rather than the runtime translator: deterministic, free,
  offline, reviewable before it ships, and plural-aware if we ever need it.
  The runtime translator stays for book strings only, because the set of book
  languages is open-ended and the set of UI languages is not.
-->
